Hi Everyone, I'm writing this email to connect you all, as it may be good for you to meet and discuss your experience/thoughts/ideas with each other! 
You are all undergraduate students I recently started to work with. 
Lakshmi and Manav are exploring how LLMs and LRMs (large reasoning models, which are LLMs trained to have elaborated thinking before responding) reason for complex code generation. A particular scenario I mentioned to Manav today is "secure code generation", i.e., generating code that does not introduce vulnerability (e.g., as specified by Common Weakness Enumeration types). See our recent study https://arxiv.org/pdf/2506.23034.
Mohan is more on the interpretability side, currently exploring an extension of our DCD paper (https://arxiv.org/pdf/2605.09129) on code generation tasks. Specifically, we want to see if LLMs similarly maintain different mechanisms, in a way different to how humans solve the task, when they do even simple coding task. 
Feel free to connect with each other and have offline chats/study groups as needed! 
Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE) is a list of software and hardware weaknesses.
 